cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use DiaBloS Modern in your research, please cite the software using
  the metadata below. Until the accompanying JOSS paper is published, please
  also cite the original DiaBloS article given under `preferred-citation`,
  which describes the block-diagram processing algorithm this tool builds on.
type: software
title: DiaBloS Modern
abstract: >-
  A desktop block-diagram simulator for dynamical systems, built with Python
  and PyQt5. Diagrams are compiled to an ODE and integrated with SciPy, with
  zero-crossing event detection, subsystems and user libraries, linearisation
  with Bode/Nyquist/root-locus/LQR analysis, Monte Carlo ensembles and
  parameter sweeps, PDE and optimization blocks, TikZ/SVG/Python export, and a
  headless command-line interface.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-09-03'
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Sapetor/diablos-modern'
url: 'https://github.com/Sapetor/diablos-modern'
keywords:
  - simulation
  - block diagram
  - control systems
  - dynamical systems
  - engineering education
  - Python
  - PyQt5
